course: dictionary
lesson: 107
title: Adjust: change a little to make it right
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To adjust something is to change it a little so that it is right or works better. You might adjust a bike seat so your legs reach the pedals, or adjust the volume so a film is not too loud. «If homework always takes far too long, a parent can talk to the teacher, who may adjust it.» The teacher changes the homework a little, so it is the right amount.
explain: Adjust also has a second meaning: to get used to a new situation. «Ella had new glasses, and it took a week to adjust to them.» Her eyes needed time to get used to the new lenses before everything felt normal.
explain: Clue words help you. Little changes, right, better and get used to all point to adjust. Ask yourself: is something being changed a little to fit, or is someone getting used to something new? Then swap in another word, like change or get used to, and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Adjust is a verb: adjust, adjusts, adjusted, adjusting.
fact: «Adjust» means to change something a little so that it is right or works better.
fact: «Adjust to» means to get used to a new situation.
fact: In a science test you adjust only one thing at a time, so you can see what made the difference.
fact: In maths you can adjust an estimate when you find a better measurement.
exercise: Mia's bike seat is too low for her. What should she do to it? | *Adjust it | Throw it away | Paint it
exercise: «If homework always takes far too long, a parent can talk to the teacher, who may adjust it.» What might the teacher do? | Make it much longer | *Change it a little so it is the right amount | Cancel the whole school day
exercise: «The volume was too loud, so Sam adjusted it down.» What did Sam do? | Made it louder | Turned it off forever | Broke the speaker | *Changed it a little to make it right
test: In a science test, why do you adjust only one thing at a time? | *So you can see what made the difference | So the teacher is happy | Because you are not allowed to adjust two things | So the test takes longer
test: What does «adjust to» mean? | To move something to a new place | To stop doing something | *To get used to a new situation | To fix something broken
exam: Which sentence uses adjust in its first meaning, to change a little so it works better? | Sam adjusted to life in a new country | *Sam turned the volume down a little so it was right | Sam ran to school | Sam was sad all day
